      "title": "Gems / Runes / Crystals"
    },
    {
      "id": "rel",
      "title": "Ancient Relics"
    },
    {
      "id": "mat",
      "title": "Cubing Materials",
      "intro": "Organs include Hearts, Souls, Brains, Eyes, Scalps, Horns, Fangs, Jawbones, Spleens, Quills and Tails. Steaks, Cookbooks and Flags are not Organs."
    },
    {
      "id": "stock",
      "title": "Stockers",
      "intro": "You can buy Stockers at Gheed. Most Stockers can store up to 2 items of a kind at once."
    },
    {
      "id": "coupon",
      "title": "Coupons"
    },
    {
      "id": "nor",
      "title": "Normal Items"
    },
    {
      "id": "mag",
      "title": "Magic / Rare Items"
    },
    {
      "id": "uni",
      "title": "Unique Items"
    },
    {
      "id": "set",
      "title": "Set Items"
    },
    {
      "id": "old",
      "title": "Legacy Craft (LoD Craft)",
      "intro": "LoD crafting recipes have been drastically improved (and made more expensive as well). No limitation for the base item: the Blood Gloves recipe accepts all gloves, for example. (ilvl = char lvl × 60% + previous ilvl × 60%)"
    },
    {
      "id": "new",
      "title": "Class Craft",
      "intro": "Class Crafted items can be used by any class, unless the base item is class specific. For example, if you play a Barbarian but need lots of IAS and Crushing Blow, you may like Necro Crafted weapons better than Barbarian Crafted weapons. Stat Forging, Rune Forging and Tab Forging are allowed for Crafted items. (ilvl = char lvl × 60% + previous ilvl × 60%)"
    },
    {
      "id": "rin",
      "title": "Rings / Amulets",
      "intro": "When you reroll multiple Amulets or Rings, the last one put in the Cube determines the type. For example, if you put a Ring, an Amazon Ring and a Sorc Ring in this order, you'll get a new Sorc Ring. If the output ilvl is lower than the level of the spawned Unique, it turns into a rare."
    },
    {
      "id": "cha",
      "title": "Charms"
    },
    {
      "id": "jew",
      "title": "Jewels"
    },
    {
      "id": "qui",
      "title": "Arrow / Bolt Quivers"
    },
    {
      "id": "for",
      "title": "Forging",
      "intro": "Forging enhances an item for no penalty, but an item may have only one Forging mod at a time. You can remove any unwanted Forging (except Wo Forging) to apply another Forging. Wo Forging can't be removed because there is no way to remove the \"Indestructible\" property."
    },
    {
      "id": "dst",
      "title": "D-Stoning",
      "intro": "D-Stoning can also be applied to unforgeable items like Runeworded items. D-Stoning can't be removed, so please apply it carefully. Every D-Stoning cap is a standalone cap: an item with 190% fire spell damage from affixes and a 200% D-Stone cap can reach 390%. The only exception is enhanced damage and enhanced defense, which cannot go above 500% on any item. D-Stoning applied to a white item after making a Runeword is lost when you remove the Runes; applied before making the Runeword, it remains. D-Stoning doesn't work if the target is elite with a +58 level requirement penalty or more, exceptional with +79 or more, or normal/jewelry with +99 or more."
    },
    {
      "id": "tin",
      "title": "Tinkering",
      "intro": "All items are generated with 25-35 invisible Tinkering points as an inherent property. Each Tinkering recipe consumes some Tinkering point(s). If an item cannot be tinkered anymore, its points have been depleted."
    },
    {
      "id": "bas",
      "title": "Base Upgrades / Changes",
      "intro": "You can't reroll Unique/Set items after a base upgrade, and you can't convert Convertible Set items after a base upgrade. Base Upgrade recipes don't accept Ethereal Armor. Use the special upgrade recipes for Mercenary Sets, which are cheaper and better."
    },
    {
      "id": "soc",
      "title": "Socket Recipes",
      "intro": "The number of sockets can't exceed the max sockets of the base item. Items dropped in Normal and Nightmare Act 1 can't have the max sockets in some cases. You can't change the number of existing sockets."
    },
    {
      "id": "sec",
      "title": "Secret Recipes",
      "intro": "Secret Recipes require a specific Ancient Scroll to be performed. Ancient Scrolls are found randomly by playing the game and can be identified using an Ancient Decipherer. The Ancient Scroll is returned after performing the recipe."
    },
    {
      "id": "tyrael",
      "title": "Tyrael's Might Extra Boon",
      "intro": "Tyrael's Might can receive additional bonuses through a unique, one-time recipe."
    }
  ],
  "hideOutputs": [
    "Red Portal",
    "Cow Portal",
    "Pandemonium Portal",
    "Pandemonium Finale Portal"
  ],
  "hideItemTypes": [
    "can1",
    "can9"
